thread:
alex: Heads-up — nsys traces for the canary show a lot of tiny unnamed ranges around kvcache prefetch that make the timeline unreadable. Thinking we should standardize on a "verb-first" short naming convention so grep and trace filters are obvious. cc @maria @junaid

maria: Yep saw that. nsys run: nsys-2026-03-02-15:12:08. The prefetch kernels scatter across the timeline because we don't mark request boundaries well. Also some ranges currently include long JSON blobs in the name (yikes). :grimacing:

junaid: Strong +1 for short stable tokens. My take: 1) keep NVTX text <= 32 chars, 2) prefer kebab or colon-separated tokens, 3) include a tiny numeric req id when available (not full UUID). Example: "kvcache:prefetch:42". Avoid interpolating large strings.

oscar: Quick example proposal for macros (cheap and alloc-free):
```c
static inline void nvtx_push_req(const char *comp, const char *verb, int reqid) {
  char buf[32];
  int n = snprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), "%s:%s:%d", comp, verb, reqid);
  if (n > 0) nvtxRangePushA(buf);
}

// usage
nvtx_push_req("kvcache", "prefetch", req_id);
// ... work ...
nvtxRangePop();
```

maria: That looks good. Two caveats: 1) snprintf can still be a bit costly on hot paths — we should benchmark overhead, 2) some places don't have req_id (background prefetch) so name should fall back to "kvcache:prefetch:bg".

alex: For the naming taxonomy, proposal: "component:action:shorttag" where action is verb (prefetch, lookup, commit), shorttag is one of {reqNN, bg, coalesced}. Keep components short: kvcache, batcher, kernel, rpc. Examples: "kvcache:lookup:req7", "batcher:flush:coalesced".

junaid: Regarding per-request spans: prefer one outer span per request ("rt:req:<id>") and then internal spans for hotspots. That way perf tools can collapse by request. And we can add attributes for model, seq_len in the NVTX payload (if we switch to NVTX attributes) instead of in the name.

maria: Good call on attributes. For now we can do names + a small integer id; later switch to nvtxRangeStartEx with nvtxEventAttributes for structured data when we need it.

perf-bot: nsys snapshot saved: s3://redwood-perf/nsys/nsys-2026-03-02-15_12_08.qdrep (auto-upload) :white_check_mark:

oscar: For immediate actionable items:
- maria -> run 2 profiles (current codebase + snprintf macro) with req id fallback and attach trimmed traces (filter component names)
- junaid -> prototype a tiny constant-pool naming approach (rotate 256 small buffers on thread-local ring to avoid snprintf for stable short names)
- alex -> update instrumentation doc with the "component:verb:tag" guideline and examples, plus the rule: "no >32 byte names, no large payloads in names"

maria: I'll run profiles today and paste a couple of perfetto links. If we can make the timeline readable we should be able to spot kernel ordering regressions and batching heuristics that swap order.

alex: SGTM. If we reduce name noise and get per-request wrappers in, nsys and perfetto will be much easier to query. :thumbsup:
